  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Chevron Usa obligated $339M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Chevron Usa received 85 awards so far, with an average award size of $4M, and obligations were up 46.7% year over year. Chevron Usa has shown a steady increase in obligations since FY21, moving from $55.8M in FY21 to $339M in FY26. Chevron Usa’s obligations concentrated in Petroleum Refineries, which accounted for $338M of obligations, while Other Warehousing and Storage accounted for $1.1M. Chevron Usa’s current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables report total contract values rather than current-year obligations. Chevron Usa’s most recent fiscal-year jump follows a rise to $231M in FY25 from $132M in FY24. Chevron Usa’s award mix and market concentration show heavy exposure to refinery-related work, with minimal activity reported in other NAICS categories. Buyers, specific contract end dates, and detailed award-value tables are not reported here, so contract-level timing and agency concentration cannot be derived from the figures provided.",
